  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.3. Increased institutional capacity and resilience of labour administrations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Damascus Chamber of Industry re-establish its OSH training centre in Adra District and provided OSH training for business operators. The ILO supported the capacity building of the members of the Damascus Chamber of Industry, General Federation of Trade Unions, as well as labour inspectorates of local administrations on OSH to qualify them as trainers in this field and enable them to provide high quality and effective relevant training to other members of their organizations as well as to workers. 
A particular support in this biennium also included the provision of PPEs and OSH equipment to the Damascus Chamber of Industry along with the training of trainers, 43 participants, to re-establish its OSH training centre in Adra District, responsible for OSH training for business operators.</narrative>
   </description>
